TCP Three-Way Handshake, Teardown and Flags
1. Why TCP needs a handshake
TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) gives reliable, ordered delivery between two programs. Before any data moves, both sides must agree to talk and must exchange their starting sequence numbers. These numbers let each side number its bytes, detect lost data and put packets back in order. The three-way handshake is how this agreement is made.
2. Three-way handshake (opening a connection)
Step
Direction
Flags
What happens
